---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Cta from '../../components/Cta.astro';
import SectionNav from '../../components/SectionNav.astro';
---
<Base title={"Keeping a Hotel Open Through a Receiver's Sale"} description={"What we handle so a hotel in receivership does not miss a night: the franchise, the management company, the liquor license, bookings, staff, and taxes."}>
  <Hero eyebrow={"For receivers and counsel"} title={"What we handle so the hotel does not miss a night."} lead={"A closed hotel loses its staff, its bookings, and often its flag. Most of the value in a receivership depends on continuous operation."} />
  <SectionNav section="receivers" />
  <main id="main">
<section class="section"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Six things that have to carry over</p><h2>The transition, area by area.</h2></div>
      <div class="cells">
        <div><h3>Franchise</h3><p>We apply to the brand for a new franchise agreement in advance of closing and address its improvement requirements directly.</p><p>The flag brings the reservation system and loyalty program that supply much of a hotel's demand.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Management</h3><p>We coordinate with the receiver's management company on staff, systems, and the handover of accounts.</p><p>A change of manager is often the first step in a recovery, so the handover is planned, not improvised.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Licenses</h3><p>We arrange the transfer of the liquor license and operating permits, with interim arrangements where the state allows.</p><p>Rules differ by state, so the timeline is built into the closing.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Bookings</h3><p>Group contracts and advance deposits are identified and honored through the transfer.</p><p>Group business and deposits are part of what the hotel is worth.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Employees</h3><p>We work with the manager so the staff the hotel depends on stay in place.</p><p>The people who know the hotel are what keep it running through a change of owner.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Taxes</h3><p>Occupancy and sales tax balances are settled at closing under the sale order.</p><p>These taxes are collected on behalf of the government and have to stay current.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">The timetable</p><h2>Before closing, at closing, and through the transfer.</h2></div>
      <div class="cells">
        <div><h3>Before closing</h3><ul><li>Apply to the brand for a new franchise agreement</li><li>Coordinate with the manager on staff, systems, and the handover of accounts</li><li>Arrange the transfer of the liquor license and operating permits</li><li>Identify group contracts and advance deposits</li></ul></div>
        <div><h3>At closing</h3><ul><li>Settle occupancy and sales tax balances under the sale order</li><li>Hand over the accounts</li><li>Transfer the hotel</li></ul></div>
        <div><h3>Through the transfer</h3><ul><li>Honor group contracts and advance deposits</li><li>Keep the staff in place</li><li>Address the brand's improvement requirements</li></ul></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="feature"><div class="wrap">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">The six points</p><h2>What decides whether a hotel stays open.</h2></div>
      <div><p class="lead">In a receivership, six points decide whether a hotel keeps operating: the order of appointment, the franchise, the liquor license, taxes, payroll and insurance, and funding. Our notes cover each of them.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-light arrow" href="/library/receivership/">Read the library note</a></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Related reading</p></div><ul class="toc"><li><a href="/blog/liquor-licenses-and-hotel-transfers/">Liquor licenses and hotel transfers: plan the timeline early <span>Blog</span></a></li><li><a href="/blog/taxes-that-can-follow-a-hotel/">Occupancy and sales taxes: the liabilities that can follow a hotel <span>Blog</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#flag">Flag <span>Glossary</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#management-agreement">Management agreement <span>Glossary</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#pip">Property improvement plan (PIP) <span>Glossary</span></a></li></ul></div></section>
  </main>
  <Cta title={"Tell us about the hotel and the case."} text={"We respond to receivers and counsel directly."} label={"Discuss a receivership"} />
</Base>
